## Context

Follow-up of 1390 (PR #2078). The author opened the d77349fe page in Firefox
on 2026-10-31 and asked for "some serious prettyfication": the page works but
reads as a raw chart. Same constraints as 1390: one self-contained file, inline
SVG/CSS/JS, no external URL, JSON export unchanged.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Header: a title (what session this is: id plus a human label such as its
      first prompt or slash command when derivable), author (the session's
      user, e.g. git `user.name`, else the host user), and date (session start;
      generation time may follow)
- [ ] One paragraph under the header saying what the page shows and how to
      read it: lanes = agents (session, subagents, seats under their parent),
      bars = calls positioned by start and sized by duration, hover for
      details, how to zoom and pan
- [ ] Lanes drawn on alternating background shades, so a row's lane is
      readable across the full width
- [ ] Mouse wheel zooms horizontally, centred on the pointer
- [ ] Click-hold-drag pans the viewport (horizontally at least)
- [ ] Existing tests still pass; the self-contained test still holds; the JSON
      export stays byte-identical
- [ ] Rendered for d77349fe-10eb-46dd-a58c-d5723e771c4d and checked in
      Firefox (headless screenshot; the author looks at interaction)

## Notes

- The session argument needs the full id today (`d77349fe` alone fails:
  "neither in the live tree nor in the archive"). Accepting a unique prefix is
  a cheap usability fix the hunt may fold in if trivial; not an exit criterion.
